WEBVTT

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:06.980
Shingetsu-chan?

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.360
Toying with people's hearts is so much fun.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.870
Wake my sister up!

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.280
Lift her curse!

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:21.700
Please...

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.580
If you'll remove her curse...

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:29.590
I'm willing to lose to you!

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.090
Really?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:44.490
<i>Magical power comes and goes 
in time with the user's heart.</i>

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:48.230
<i>It changes so easily from 
one color to the next.</i>

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.780
<i>Red, blue, yellow, ultramarine...</i>

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.490
<i>What color is your magic?</i>

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.990
What? Is this...

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.210
Kuon-chan!

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.080
Welcome...

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:46.000
<b>GRANBELM</b>

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:45.790
The Two Princeps

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:06.620
Where am I?

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:15.670
Huh?

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.800
Onee-chan...

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:19.550
Kuon-chan?

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.960
Wait! Wait, wait!

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.380
Kuon-chan! Kuon-chan!

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.730
You're...

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.110
What did you do?

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:33.020
Nothing!

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:36.650
Whoa! Wait! Give me half! Give me half!

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.740
No!

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.240
Why did we come back to 
your place, Shingetsu-chan?

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.490
You didn't "come back" here.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:50.940
If you're not envisioning where you 
want to return to when the battle ends,

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:53.930
you're sent back to the 
place you entered it from.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.330
Oh...

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.540
And you're returned naked.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.880
When you want to go back, 
you need to envision

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.310
where you're going back to 
and what you were wearing.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.640
Tell us that sooner!

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.020
What is it?

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.100
How did the battle end? 
What happened to Anna-san?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.600
I told you that I wouldn't lose to her.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:19.370
The core of her ARMANOX 
was completely destroyed,

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.570
which means she's been 
removed from GRANBELM.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:27.530
I'm sure she'll understand someday.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.290
Oh, it's Nene-chan.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.040
What'd she say?

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.040
The pig

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:36.960
"The pig"?

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.040
Bring it to me

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.470
And... there.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.990
Oh, wow!

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.680
DROSELA NOCTURNE.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.740
Judging from its calm movements here,

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.170
it's clearly not fighting at full strength.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:00.340
What family is its mage from?

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.190
I think her name was... Suishou?

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:06.280
Suishou? Never heard of her.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:09.490
And there's no record of this mech 
being used in past GRANBELM battles.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.330
She lived at Anna-san's house, right?

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.800
Apparently.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.090
Based on their relationship,

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:17.510
she doesn't seem to be from 
a very large mage family.

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:18.960
I see.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.210
What about this "Anna" girl, then?

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.680
What mage family is she from?

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.320
Her family? You know who she is.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.930
The one who piloted ACONITE GRIS.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.970
What ARMANOX is that?

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:38.020
It's red, and it was handed 
down in the Fugo family.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.460
You fought it, remember?

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.120
The Fugo family?

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:46.360
That bloodline was defeated 
before I was, wasn't it?

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.440
She lost her memories?

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.540
It definitely seems that way.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.380
She's lost all her memories 
of Anna's existence.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.130
Why?

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:06.550
Some kind of magic that was too powerful 
for a mage's life force to endure

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:07.850
wiped them out.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.900
You mean...

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.350
Any idea how it happened?

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:15.880
You know, don't you?

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.810
I haven't made certain of it, but...

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:23.180
In the end, I saw light 
spreading within my mind,

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.650
then it vanished.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:26.910
It was Anna's light.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:31.350
But how could people 
forget her just like that?

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:32.980
Magic...

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:37.620
All memories and records involving 
Anna have been erased.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:40.800
After we all fought,

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.190
powerful magic intervened in this world

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:49.050
to make it as though her 
death never happened.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:50.780
Magic?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.540
Onee-sama!

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.630
Onee-sama, hurry up!

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:01.480
C'mon, what are you doing? Let's go!

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.740
Calm down.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:05.900
I'll be right there.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.890
Come on! We're going to be late!

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.910
You're not forgetting anything, are you?

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.910
Shingetsu-chan...

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:20.790
I'm all set! Hurry up or
we'll leave you behind!

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:19.610
Anna...

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:22.770
Shingetsu-chan!

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.700
Nothing you say will change the truth.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.050
White...

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:47.520
No... No! No!

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:52.840
Is something wrong?

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:55.510
No.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.590
Magical signatures? But there aren't any.

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.940
There must be something,

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:10.420
if what those girls said is true.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:15.180
Is there any chance that they saw 
some kind of illusion in that space?

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.590
It's possible, of course. But...

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:19.640
What?

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.450
You can go to bed.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:24.690
Half the reason I'm doing 
this is because I enjoy it.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:27.600
Knock it off.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:29.510
You should get some sleep.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:31.030
You're still too little.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:35.380
So... who do you think is going to win?

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:38.200
In GRANBELM.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:43.960
Onee-chan...

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.010
Onee-chan's smell...

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:52.150
Onee-chan's sound...

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.870
Shingetsu-chan...

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.660
Nice to meet you.

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:18.330
I'm Hakamada Suishou.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.460
Hiya!

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:21.910
Suishou's there?

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:26.060
<i>Well, just try to keep your distance.</i>

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.560
<i>Getting mixed up with her 
would be dangerous.</i>

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.670
Okay. But why is she...

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:32.660
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:35.880
<i>But it's clear she's after something.</i>

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:39.180
<i>How did her battle with Kuon end?</i>

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.470
The battle...

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:44.720
Uh, well...

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:46.890
Anyway, are you doing okay?

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:51.680
<i>I know I shouldn't say this lightly, but...</i>

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:55.020
<i>Don't blame yourself, okay?</i>

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:58.490
Thanks.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:20.100
You're not allowed to use 
smartphones at school.

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:25.070
Stuck the landing!

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:26.810
Wh-What do you want?

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:33.370
Were you that scared when you 
talked to that "Kuon" girl, too?

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:36.380
You three fought together, didn't you?

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:40.120
Which means I'll be all by 
myself in the next battle.

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:41.660
That's so unfair.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:45.280
Why don't you team up with me next time?

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:50.670
If you'll make me a mage, I'll use 
magic to grant any wish you want.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:53.930
I don't have any wishes,

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:56.100
and I don't even want to be a mage.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:58.740
Then why are you fighting?

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:00.720
For Shingetsu-chan!

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:01.750
Why?

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:03.260
Because I like her!

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:06.990
And I want to help make her wish come true!

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:10.680
I don't care if it's unfair. You can 
call it underhanded if you want.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:11.900
Because that's...

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:13.770
my only wish!

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:18.240
Is that really true?

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.870
What do you mean?

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:21.440
Who knows?

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:23.660
Well, that's fine... for now, anyway.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.010
Why did you do what you did?

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:30.680
You cursed Kuon-chan's 
sister, too, didn't you?

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:37.420
But... when you were fighting her, 
you... teased her like that...

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:43.720
Want to try it, too?

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:48.430
Don't make such a scary face.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.870
It's because I like both of them.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.000
You like them?

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.190
Yep.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.540
Both Shisui and Kuon.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:01.360
Let me give you just one piece 
of advice, Kohinata Mangetsu.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:02.920
What?

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:07.140
You shouldn't involve yourself 
in GRANBELM anymore.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.290
You're not cut out for it.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:14.510
You have nothing, after all.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:18.440
Nothing.

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:36.690
I'm impressed you stopped.

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:42.040
But it makes sense that you 
did. I know you love me.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:44.350
What did you do?

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:47.100
What did you do to me?!

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.450
Not a thing.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.910
I just ate a little bit...

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:57.020
of your sister Shisui's soul.

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:09.410
That's why you sense so much

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:15.060
of your sister's scent, her voice, 
and her magic in this body.

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:19.530
See? You want me to hug you, don't you?

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:21.690
You want me to hold you close, don't you?

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.850
You want me to look at you, don't you?

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.780
Come, Kuon...

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:33.790
Give it back!

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:40.960
Give my sister's soul back!

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.970
I'm ba—Oh.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.650
You'll get even smaller if you 
keep pulling all-nighters.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.800
There has to be something! There has to be!

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:55.440
Magic interference? But the 
numbers are super low.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:14:00.620
If either we or the other girls were 
having our memories altered by magic,

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:02.300
these numbers wouldn't be possible.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:06.670
Doesn't that just confirm none of you
 are being manipulated, then?

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:11.690
There are still records of inconsistencies 
in the memories of participants.

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:15.070
Apparently the cause was never found...

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.870
And you want to find it.

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.900
Obviously!

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:26.090
You actually like those 
girls quite a bit, huh?

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:28.800
Yeah, I do.

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:32.900
They all have their own reasons 
for taking part in this battle.

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:35.810
Well, then...

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.880
I need to put this stuff in the fridge.

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:52.490
Noise canceling...

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:53.500
Huh?

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:55.610
To counter powerful magic,

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:58.710
you'd generate the inverse of 
that magic to cancel it out.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.780
You can do that?

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:02.580
It's normally impossible, of course.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:07.210
But for someone capable of 
using really powerful magic...

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:10.840
For example, a being that's 
like a mass of magical power,

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:13.550
made of all the sealed magic in the world...

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:23.060
What is this?

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:24.480
Magic factors...

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:29.280
These numbers wouldn't have been possible 
even a thousand years before mages lived!

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:32.830
But all the magic in the 
world is sealed, right?

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:34.180
In Magiaconatus?

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.730
That's the accepted theory.

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:40.300
But something that could cause 
this many magic interferences

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.540
could create whatever kind 
of "history" it wanted.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.190
This signal's stronger than all the others!

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:02.890
You have nothing.

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:05.390
Don't think about it! Don't think about it!

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:06.900
That's exactly what she wants.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.280
<b>Picture Journal 
</b>Memories

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.280
<b>Grade 5 Class 4   Kohinata Mangetsu</b>

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:20.000
Huh?

00:16:21.220 --> 00:16:23.460
Huh? Huh? Huh?!

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.680
Shingetsu-chan

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.680
Are you awake?

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.340
I said you didn't have to do this...

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:55.910
It's okay. I wanted to go 
out for a walk, anyway.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:00.310
Did everything go all right with Suishou?

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:01.360
Yeah.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.710
She said a lot of things, but I'm fine.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.280
What things?

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:09.260
Oh... Well, nothing that important.

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:13.340
You're lying.

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:16.480
I can tell by looking at you.

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:22.310
Well, if you get to say 
that... you're lying, too.

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:24.080
Me?

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:24.880
Yeah.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.440
Tear tracks.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:35.830
You loved Anna-san, didn't you?

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:39.360
I don't have the right to cry.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:43.500
I'm sure she still hates me.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:45.710
Even so...

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:49.310
I'll still keep supporting you.

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:52.980
No matter how much you blame yourself,

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:55.420
I don't think it was your fault.

00:17:59.000 --> 00:17:59.890
Mangetsu...

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:00.900
Yes?

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:05.080
Please drop out of GRANBELM.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:05.750
Huh?

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:08.480
I don't want to involve you any further.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:11.270
There's no reason, nor any 
need, for you to fight.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:14.990
Because I have nothing, right?

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:16.930
Mangetsu...

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:21.360
Suishou told me that, too.

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:25.480
She told me to drop out
 because I have nothing.

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:27.160
That I'm not cut out for it.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:29.500
No! What I'm saying is...

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.160
I know.

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:34.840
I know that wasn't what 
you were trying to say.

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:52.480
It hurts... watching you fight.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:57.360
The rest of us have been 
hurt, lost something,

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:01.430
grown obsessed, or carried some 
burden that kept us fighting.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:04.030
We had no choice but to fight.

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:07.360
Fighting and becoming mages was all we had.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.750
But you...

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:15.880
You're wrong. Having nothing is my burden.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:21.580
It's white and invisible. 
It's literally nothing, but it's so heavy.

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:23.580
That's the burden I carry.

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:25.990
Just like the rest of you,

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:28.290
I want to do something with it.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:31.020
That's why I've kept fighting.

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:38.320
Tear tracks.

00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:47.060
That may be how you feel,

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:52.540
but I don't think that's true,
no matter what happens.

00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:56.500
So we're the same.

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:58.560
I guess we are.

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:02.580
Then... I still want to fight with you!

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:06.790
I can, right?

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:13.290
I let you spoil me too much.

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:15.370
Well, the same goes for me.

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:30.130
Onee-chan...

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:36.850
You and I are the strongest.

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.430
The strongest?

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:42.300
Yes. Your lightness and my heaviness...

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:47.240
By putting them together, 
we can control everything.

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.170
Onee-chan...

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:56.020
Onee-chan?

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:59.570
Wait... please...

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:01.570
Suishou...

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:04.120
Suishou?

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:08.780
Please...

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:21.450
Morning!

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:22.150
Morning.

00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:23.530
Always nice to see you.

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:26.320
Are you two planning to gang up on me?

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:27.390
That's not fair.

00:21:27.590 --> 00:21:29.760
I would settle for one-on-one.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.970
But I don't see anything wrong 
with ganging up on someone

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:35.850
who toys with people's hearts for fun.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:38.060
My, you've grown so defiant.

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:39.270
Is that a problem?

00:21:39.930 --> 00:21:41.200
Nope.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:43.710
That just makes things more interesting.

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:45.420
It'll be more fun to break you.

00:21:56.850 --> 00:21:58.050
<i>That girl...</i>

00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:02.250
<i>Even for someone who enters
 Magiaconatus and fights,</i>

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:05.030
<i>the numbers on these magic 
interferences are too extreme.</i>

00:22:05.740 --> 00:22:06.670
<i>Plus...</i>

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:10.930
<i>Here, too...</i>

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:15.900
Oh, Nene-chan!

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:26.940
<b>To be continued</b>

00:23:56.950 --> 00:23:59.580
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:57.840 --> 00:24:03.210
<i>All Kuon wants is a peaceful life 
with her older sister, Shisui.</i>

00:24:03.530 --> 00:24:08.880
<i>A crystalline laugh echoes 
tauntingly over these two sisters,</i>

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:12.470
<i>who have been toyed with all their lives 
for being born into a mage family.</i>

00:24:12.700 --> 00:24:15.930
<i>Kuon's fight to get her sister 
back is about to begin.</i>

00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:18.640
<i>Next time on </i>GRANBELM<i>,</i>

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:21.390
<b>NOCTURNE Changes Colors</b>

00:24:18.870 --> 00:24:21.080
<i>"NOCTURNE Changes Colors."</i>

00:24:21.750 --> 00:24:25.180
<i>"I wished for that curse..."</i>

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:29.980
<b>Look forward to the next episode!</b>
